WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.220 --> 00:00:05.800
Terminator: Dark Fate features some familiar
faces, not just from the beloved action sci-fi

00:00:05.800 --> 00:00:08.140
franchise, but from other films and TV shows.

00:00:08.140 --> 00:00:13.280
Linda Hamilton and Arnold Schwarzenegger are
joined by a few newcomers you just might recognize

00:00:13.280 --> 00:00:15.240
from both the big and small screens.

00:00:15.800 --> 00:00:21.080
While it may seem difficult to separate Hamilton
from the role of Sarah Connor - badass action

00:00:21.090 --> 00:00:26.550
icon and protagonist of the first two Terminator
movies - she's had memorable roles both before

00:00:26.550 --> 00:00:29.080
and after 1984's The Terminator.

00:00:29.080 --> 00:00:34.660
She starred as Vicky in the 1984 horror film
Children of the Corn, and, between 1987 and

00:00:34.660 --> 00:00:39.680
1990, she starred opposite Ron Perlman on
CBS' Beauty and the Beast.

00:00:39.680 --> 00:00:44.980
In 1997, she starred with Pierce Brosnan and
Jaime Renée Smith in the disaster thriller

00:00:44.980 --> 00:00:46.480
hit Dante's Peak.

00:00:46.480 --> 00:00:51.120
She hit the small screen in a big way in 2010,
appearing on two episodes of Weeds and scoring

00:00:51.120 --> 00:00:55.860
a recurring role on NBC's Chuck as a CIA agent
and Chuck's estranged mother.

00:00:55.860 --> 00:01:00.920
In recent years, she's nabbed a recurring
antagonist spot on Syfy's Defiance and a prominent

00:01:00.920 --> 00:01:03.700
guest role on the supernatural drama Lost
Girl.

00:01:05.320 --> 00:01:06.440
"I'll be back."

00:01:11.260 --> 00:01:16.560
The athletic woman we see going head-to-head
with the new Terminator in the teaser is Grace,

00:01:16.570 --> 00:01:18.020
played by Mackenzie Davis.

00:01:18.020 --> 00:01:22.550
As of her appearance in Dark Fate, Davis'
professional film acting career is just under

00:01:22.550 --> 00:01:23.550
a decade old.

00:01:23.550 --> 00:01:28.740
Her first starring film role came in 2013
with the romantic drama Breathe In.

00:01:28.740 --> 00:01:33.670
She appeared as Miles Teller's friend and
eventual love interest in 2014's That Awkward

00:01:33.670 --> 00:01:34.320
Moment.

00:01:34.320 --> 00:01:39.359
Davis' tireless engineer Mindy Park played
a key role in getting Matt Damon's astronaut

00:01:39.360 --> 00:01:41.780
Mark home in 2015's The Martian.

00:01:41.780 --> 00:01:47.200
Mindy Park wasn't her last nerdy role - from
2014 to 2017, she played programmer Cameron

00:01:47.200 --> 00:01:49.440
on AMC's Halt and Catch Fire.

00:01:49.440 --> 00:01:55.039
She achieved even more small screen exposure
when she starred alongside Gugu Mbatha-Raw

00:01:55.040 --> 00:01:59.680
in "San Junipero," hailed by many as the finest
episode of Black Mirror.

00:01:59.680 --> 00:02:04.219
If you're excited for Terminator: Dark Fate,
you may have already caught another long-awaited

00:02:04.220 --> 00:02:08.240
science fiction sequel dealing with complex
questions about artificial intelligence.

00:02:08.240 --> 00:02:13.440
That brings us to one of Mackenzie Davis'
most prominent roles to date: Mariette, a

00:02:13.440 --> 00:02:16.400
replicant freedom fighter in Blade Runner
2049.

00:02:17.460 --> 00:02:22.760
Terminator: Dark Fate introduces us to Rev
9, an advanced Terminator model played by

00:02:22.760 --> 00:02:27.300
Gabriel Luna, who you should definitely recognize
if you're a Marvel TV fan.

00:02:27.300 --> 00:02:32.920
Luna appeared in the fourth season of Marvel's
Agents of S.H.I.E.L.D. as Robbie Reyes, a.k.a.

00:02:32.920 --> 00:02:35.200
the supernatural vigilante Ghost Rider.

00:02:35.200 --> 00:02:39.959
Over his season-long arc, Reyes - having been
granted the power of the Spirit of Vengeance

00:02:39.959 --> 00:02:42.900
after getting murdered by a street gang - helps
S.H.I.E.L.D.

00:02:42.900 --> 00:02:46.620
tackle a few supernatural threats before exiting
the show with the season 4 finale.

00:02:46.620 --> 00:02:51.280
Before playing Ghost Rider, Luna starred in
ABC's short-lived crime procedural Wicked

00:02:51.280 --> 00:02:53.920
City as Detective Paco Contreras.

00:02:53.920 --> 00:02:58.960
Fans of the El Rey Network may also recognize
him as Tony Bravo, the soccer star who doubles

00:02:58.960 --> 00:03:01.100
as a CIA operative in Matador.

00:03:01.100 --> 00:03:06.239
He appeared in 2011's dark comedy Bernie - the
real life story of a mortician who befriends

00:03:06.239 --> 00:03:10.630
and later murders an eccentric millionaire
- and starred alongside Johnny Simmons and

00:03:10.630 --> 00:03:16.549
Clifton Collins Jr. in the 2016 thriller Transpecos,
the story of border patrol agents embroiled

00:03:16.549 --> 00:03:18.600
in a conflict against a drug cartel.

00:03:19.120 --> 00:03:24.520
The woman who Grace and Sarah Connor are risking
everything to protect is Dani Ramos.

00:03:24.520 --> 00:03:29.680
Dani is played by Natalia Reyes, a Colombian
actress whose fame has yet to find a sure

00:03:29.680 --> 00:03:33.560
foothold with American audiences, but whose
talents have already made her a star in her

00:03:33.560 --> 00:03:34.560
native country.

00:03:34.560 --> 00:03:39.640
Reyes is perhaps best known for her starring
role in the Colombian telenovela Lady, La

00:03:39.650 --> 00:03:45.620
Vendedora de Rosas, the fascinating and tragic
true story of Lady Maria Tabares, a famous

00:03:45.620 --> 00:03:49.920
Colombian actress who was sentenced to 26
years in prison for ordering the murder of

00:03:49.920 --> 00:03:51.280
a taxicab driver.

00:03:51.280 --> 00:03:56.219
More recently, Reyes starred in the critically-hailed
crime epic Birds of Passage, which gained

00:03:56.220 --> 00:03:59.500
her much more international attention, including
in the States.

00:03:59.980 --> 00:04:02.440
We hope Arnold Schwarzenegger looks familiar.

00:04:02.440 --> 00:04:06.520
If he doesn't, hey, we're not judging, but
it's just kind of a mystery why you're interested

00:04:06.520 --> 00:04:08.420
in Terminator: Dark Fate at all.

00:04:08.420 --> 00:04:11.500
Maybe you thought it was a really hardcore
pest control service?

00:04:11.500 --> 00:04:12.700
We don't know.

00:04:12.700 --> 00:04:17.540
Schwarzenegger's first film was his starring
role in 1970's Hercules in New York.

00:04:17.540 --> 00:04:23.120
His prominence as the action hero of the eighties
began with 1984's Conan the Barbarian, in

00:04:23.120 --> 00:04:26.460
which he played the savage warrior of Robert
E. Howard's fiction.

00:04:26.460 --> 00:04:31.080
That same year he starred as the ruthless
cyborg hunting Sarah Connor in James Cameron's

00:04:31.080 --> 00:04:35.300
The Terminator, truly cementing his status
as a pop culture icon.

00:04:35.760 --> 00:04:37.180
"I'll be back."

00:04:37.340 --> 00:04:41.940
Ironically, while the first Terminator film
did so much for his career, he didn't play

00:04:41.940 --> 00:04:43.400
bad guys much after that.

00:04:43.400 --> 00:04:48.360
Throughout the '80s and '90s, he battled mercenaries
in Commando, hunted a monster in The Predator,

00:04:48.370 --> 00:04:53.910
won a deadly game show in The Running Man,
got his ass to Mars in Total Recall, and failed

00:04:53.910 --> 00:04:57.260
to keep the wool over Jamie Lee Curtis' eyes
in True Lies.

00:04:57.700 --> 00:05:02.980
Through it all, he made the delivery of violent
yet corny one-liners into an art all its own.

00:05:02.980 --> 00:05:07.630
As he grew in fame, he was successful in a
couple of memorable comedies as well, namely

00:05:07.630 --> 00:05:11.520
1988's Twins and 1990's Kindergarten Cop.

00:05:11.520 --> 00:05:16.680
More recently, Schwarzenegger has been a regular
fixture in the Expendables franchise and turned

00:05:16.680 --> 00:05:21.300
in a surprisingly subtle performance in 2015's
low-key zombie drama Maggie.

00:05:21.300 --> 00:05:27.140
Oh yeah, and between 2003 and 2011, he was
busy being the 38th governor of California.

